---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  ["local-first", "Local-first operation"],
  ["optional-services", "Optional services"],
  ["third-parties", "Third-party providers"],
  ["controls", "Your controls"],
  ["changes", "Changes"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy — shuv2code"
  description="How the local-first shuv2code project handles data."
  heading="shuv2code Privacy Notice"
  lede="shuv2code is an open-source, local-first application maintained by shuv1337. This notice describes the software's default behavior; it does not invent a hosted service or corporate data controller."
  effectiveDate="2026-07-28"
  lastUpdated="2026-07-28"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="local-first">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Local-first operation</h2>
    <p>
      By default, shuv2code stores its application state in <code>.shuv2code</code> on systems you
      control and connects to coding-agent runtimes you configure. The project does not receive your
      prompts, repositories, credentials, agent output, or local telemetry merely because you run the
      software.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="optional-services">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>Optional services</h2>
    <p>
      Hosted connection, authentication, updates, notifications, and observability code is disabled
      unless an operator explicitly configures it. If you enable one of those integrations, the
      operator of the endpoint you configured is responsible for describing its data practices.
      shuv2code does not ship a default shuv1337-hosted endpoint.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-parties">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>Third-party providers</h2>
    <p>
      Agent, model, source-control, identity, notification, and distribution providers process data
      under their own terms. Review their policies and configure their retention and training
      controls before using confidential or personal information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="controls">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Your controls</h2>
    <p>
      You control the machines, endpoints, credentials, and providers connected to shuv2code. You can
      inspect the source, disable integrations, revoke provider credentials, and remove the
      <code>.shuv2code</code> directory to erase local application state. Legacy <code>.t3</code>
      state is never read, migrated, warned about, or deleted by shuv2code.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      Material changes to this notice are tracked in the repository. A distributor or hosted-service
      operator may need a separate notice for its own processing.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
